            "review_title": "Review at Bun Bo Hue Gia Dinh",
            "review_text": "Sarah K\nPeppermint Grove, Australia30 contributions\n0\nFirst stop of our Xo tour and delicious\nJun 2016 • Couples\nWe were brought here as part of the Xo tour and the food is delicious.\n\nIt feels like a local secret. The broth is simply delicious but be careful when adding the chilli - you don't need much to get a kick!\n\nYou add some local vegetables - bean sprouts, shredded banana flower and a local Vietnamese water green... yeah I can't remember what it's called.\n\nWe were reminded several times that it's not Pho. The noodles are round not flat. And traditionally it's a beef broth. \n\nI haven't had this dish before so I can't compare it to others but it seemed an excellent example to me. :)\n\nA great start to the tour.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 11, 2016",
