            "review_title": "Review at Bun Bo Hue Gia Dinh",
            "review_text": "minhphuong10\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nThe best Hue Beef Noodle in Ho Chi Minh city with only VND30,000\nMar 2016 • Friends\nHue beef noodle takes its origin from the Royal Hue City of Central Vietnam. The broth is from cooking beef bones for a long period of time as well as a variety of different spices including lemongrass.\nHow does it taste? Well, having a bowl of Hue beef noodle, you will easily recognize that it is completely different from Pho since the former’s beef broth is much more spicy.\nA typical version of Hue beef noodle must include pork, roast beef, Vietnamese salami, Hue’s style salami, shrimp sauce and chopped lettuce.\nYou are in Ho Chi Minh, and wondering if such a Hue’s specialty appears in Ho Chi Minh city or not. You should refer to the following reliable address \n• “Bun bo hue Gia Dinh” at 469 Bach Dang St., Binh Thanh Dist, Ho Chi Minh (near Ba Chieu market)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 3, 2016",
